# Layout & visual gate before handoff

**Passing logic ≠ passing layout.** Filter counts, API responses, and CDP/JS metrics **do not** satisfy UI completion if alignment, spacing, nesting, or overflow were not **seen** in a real browser.

Read **`browser-first-mandatory.mdc`** first. This rule adds the **layout** bar on top of interaction/behavior checks in **`verify-ui-before-done.mdc`**.

## Hard gate

Before **done**, **fixed**, **verified**, or **ready for review** on any user-visible UI change:

### 1. Two viewports (both required when layout changed)

| Viewport | Width | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Mobile** | ≤749px (or device emulation) | Always for nav, drawers, filters, collection sidebars |
| **Desktop** | ≥990px | Always when desktop layout exists (vertical facets, mega menu, wide grids) |

Skipping either viewport = **incomplete handoff** unless the change is explicitly single-viewport-only (state which one in the reply).

### 2. Screenshot evidence (mandatory)

Capture **at least one screenshot per viewport** showing the **changed surface**:

- Default state (panel open / filters visible / menu expanded as relevant)
- After interaction state when expand/collapse or drill-down affects layout

**Attach or reference** screenshots in the final reply. Describe what a customer would **see** (alignment, indent, wrapping), not only what code changed.

### 3. Layout checklist (eyeball — not grep)

For every new or changed UI surface, confirm visually:

- [ ] Checkbox/control **touching or aligned with** its label (no floating columns)
- [ ] Nested hierarchy **stacks vertically** (parent above children), not side-by-side columns
- [ ] Indent is **consistent** per depth level (no stair-step drift)
- [ ] Text **does not break mid-word** or clip off-container (`Char's Counterattack`, long series names)
- [ ] No orphan rows (labels without controls, controls without labels)
- [ ] Spacing matches surrounding Dawn/facet patterns (not raw unstyled HTML)

If any item fails → **keep fixing** until a fresh screenshot passes.

## Does NOT count as layout verification

- `Invoke-WebRequest`, HTML grep, or “marker found in page source”
- CDP-only checks (element counts, `getBoundingClientRect` gaps) **without** a screenshot you inspected
- “Tests pass” / manifest verify / filter count math alone
- Opening the wrong URL, wrong theme (`preview_theme_id` missing on AI Dev work), or homepage only
- Describing expected layout from code review

## Final reply must include a **Layout verification** block

**Literal heading required:** the user-facing reply **must** contain this exact markdown heading (level-3):

```markdown
### Layout verification
```

Without that heading, the handoff is **incomplete** for any user-visible UI change.

```markdown
### Layout verification
| Viewport | URL | Screenshot | Pass/fail |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Mobile 390px | … | Grade + series filters, nested under SD/HG | Pass — checkbox beside label |
| Desktop 1400px | … | Left facet column | Pass — children indented one level |
```

Each row must name the **URL**, what the **screenshot shows**, and **pass/fail** for layout (alignment, nesting, wrapping) — not only behavior counts.

If blocked (no browser, auth, theme push failed): use the same heading and set pass/fail to **Not verified — blocked**; do **not** imply the UI looks correct.

## Forbidden handoff language (UI changes)

Do **not** use these words/phrases in the final reply unless **`### Layout verification`** is present with at least one populated row (or explicit **Not verified — blocked**):

- done / complete / finished
- fixed / resolved
- verified / confirmed / looks good / works
- ready for review / ready to test / ship it / live

**Allowed without layout block:** API-only, backend-only, or refactors with **zero** user-visible layout change — say so explicitly (“no UI layout change; layout gate N/A”).

## User reject phrase

If the agent omits **`### Layout verification`**, the user may reply: **“Layout gate not met — send screenshots at 390px and 1400px.”** Treat that as a hard stop; do not argue that counts or tests were enough.

